<description>&lt;p&gt;The rebuilt flood-damaged town is being promoted as a showcase for the Libyan strongman’s rule, while Fezzan Revolutionaries Force continues to contest Haftar’s control in southern Libya. The House of Representatives condemned the armed closure of Zintan Airport that stalled a parliamentary session, and the UN welcomed new laws criminalising the conscription of minors and raising the recruitment age to 18. Libya seized large quantities of drug pills and cocaine as trafficking networks expand, and the parliament faced clashes over sessions in Zintan and attacks on the new presidency in Dabaiba. The Libyan zoo welcomed its first white-tiger cub months after reopening. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxOUF92cEV2aUZOZTdpZzRjNVk1dzVCTjhkaUVGODZyem1EQzhvckhpNkc3a3FseW1JVzdZTmFyWEcyMU03Z2RoWnZxUmt0ZWtFZFJXMzlMWmtzM3JhVWJ5c0ZwTTVKcWVsODhjS1I4X21laFFaeVZMY3drUUliLUlDT21kMnpYQ0hjQ2JfQlVnbkVpMDlvSERvNkwxaU5BWkUzYmpXbWdPSk1VdmpFLWhPMjQ0YXhQaFBGUERuNW04WjhpdVU?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxQZzNVX2NPYXpBVE1pZmVJOEdPcnJJeVYtcW5LTThGcHNuWFY5dnFFQXZhUGdxQURCd00wWndoVWdGNGRxM0xPOUR4T3IwVVNyXzl4enl0dlB1OHV0N0xvSlJ2d2JVaUJZbjJFYnJSX0Z1NkJ1dmRJSXk4NWxwRjV0Z29ZUkJJQmJIQWJ2end0TGpDc1ppcDZ2ZG54T0NWYkVlNWRKOE1R?oc=5&quot;&gt;Somali Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE1LNWtaVkVtaWR5blozTVduaVhRQXp2UEJhakxwMHhERGpxN2dxSmJzWnpRVktBWHllUWRGb1VacnZlTDFidGxCamNCUWNlQVdTZFpRRnVPM181aEE5TXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxPU250c2FyQkIxOXZHaUxLbzRMRlpGTi1jOXRBeXVTdzNiZ0F3REc0VmVjTmlYXzRaU3hJMHZGaEc5RHF2TGNvRXgySHY0cEkxc1pMNUpkOVJmQ1dBNlhXMnJOTTlhUVItYktDb